# Each real app route gets an explicit rewrite to the SPA shell so a direct
# load/refresh works. Deliberately NOT a blanket "/*" catch-all: that was
# serving every URL, including typos and dead links, as HTTP 200 — a soft
# 404 that tells search engines a broken page is a real one. Routes below
# must be kept in sync with index.js's router.on({...}) table.
/                /index.html   200
/marvel          /index.html   200
/about           /index.html   200
/comments/*      /index.html   200
/login           /index.html   200
/signup          /index.html   200
/profile         /index.html   200
/my-list         /index.html   200
/games           /index.html   200
/theaters        /index.html   200
/tv              /index.html   200
/hot-takes       /index.html   200
/discover        /index.html   200
/movies          /index.html   200
/releases        /index.html   200
/news            /index.html   200

# Anything else (typos, old dead links, bot-probed paths) falls through to
# Netlify's real 404 instead of being disguised as a valid page.
